<p>Iran has launched large-scale missile and drone attacks over the past two days on Gulf cities including Dubai and Abu Dhabi in the UAE, Doha in Qatar, and sites in Bahrain, and it also struck U.S. military facilities elsewhere in the region, according to multiple reports. Officials cited by multiple outlets said the Gulf attacks killed at least four people and injured more than 100, with damage that included airport disruptions and strikes—or debris from interceptions—hitting civilian areas. Several reports describe the strikes as retaliation as U.S. and Israeli operations against Iran continue. TIME reported that President Donald Trump ordered a “massive and ongoing” campaign aimed at removing Iran’s regime, and it also reported that Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei was killed in U.S.-Israeli strikes—claims that remain disputed and unclear. Iran’s own reported casualties from the U.S. and Israeli bombing are described as substantially higher, with Iranian state media citing the Red Crescent in reporting at least 201 people killed—figures TIME said it could not independently verify. Even with the grim toll, Gulf air defenses reportedly intercepted many incoming projectiles. Across the region, the immediate focus has shifted to protecting civilians, securing critical infrastructure such as airports, and preventing the crisis from spreading further.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/AH2c79SvB86YJSc3gRyKiQp0tHSr8mDo4fpcJjK_Gqop9YJDI2Z53OdqcFo0rI7xcMHVTt4bK9I9ORgS8NPYZsKPzLuT9Ciu-_mLT7mbMBR0vCnI0F8AfhMlN6fyjiDrYXuIiUc_h7Dg8SI9OT7Q84cVxzBRo_SxUORv2P4heOhzPn5qXfwftGRBGEZDKOGtU660UWhBirYRRSh6KE9HmBW1lUNt4HfKM_HUp7KTFGPYdLS7DlaI5yNM' alt='A plume of smoke from an Iranian strike rising in the distance from the Dubai International Airport.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Scale of fire: Government reports cited by The New York Times said Iran fired nearly 400 missiles and more than 800 drones across the Persian Gulf over two days.</li><li>Civilian areas struck: TIME said missiles, drones, and debris from interceptions hit civilian sites including five-star resorts in Dubai and apartment buildings in Bahrain, denting the Gulf’s image of stability.</li><li>Broader theater: The BBC said Iran also launched missiles and drones toward Israel, while striking four Gulf Arab countries that host U.S. military bases.</li><li>Shelter and landmark damage: Euronews said residents took shelter in basements as strikes and debris damaged sites in Dubai and Abu Dhabi, including the Burj Al Arab; UAE officials said air defenses intercepted hundreds of projectiles.</li><li>Iran’s arsenal: Al Jazeera said Iran’s retaliation has relied on a mix of ballistic missiles and drones, used against Israel and Gulf states that host U.S. bases.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Arab Emirates: The UAE closed its embassy in Tehran and recalled its ambassador after the Gulf attacks, in what was described as the strongest condemnation yet by a Gulf state since the barrage began. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uae-closes-embassy-in-iran-after-several-killed-in-attacks-across-the-gulf/article70692876.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media/Red Crescent: Iranian state media, citing the Red Crescent, said more than 700 people were injured in Iran by U.S. and Israeli strikes and put the death toll in the hundreds—figures TIME said it could not independently verify. (<a href='https://time.com/7381884/iran-missiles-dubai-palm-gulf/'>TIME</a>)</li><li>New York Times visual investigations: A Times investigation concluded Iranian strikes exploited vulnerabilities at U.S. military locations in the region, including sites in Dubai and Bahrain. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/01/world/middleeast/iran-strikes-us-military-facilities.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>UAE authorities: Euronews said residents took shelter during alerts as damage was reported in Dubai and Abu Dhabi, including at the Burj Al Arab. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/01/iranian-strikes-hit-dubai-and-abu-dhabi-damaging-airport-terminals-and-the-burj-al-arab'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://time.com/7381884/iran-missiles-dubai-palm-gulf/'>Iran’s Retaliatory Strikes Challenge Image of Gulf Stability</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/iran-launches-drone-and-missile-strikes-across-gulf-countries-in-retaliation/'>Iran launches drone and missile strikes across Gulf countries in retaliation</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/01/world/middleeast/iran-attacks-dubai-persian-gulf-countries-retaliation.html'>Iran Attacks Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Qatar and Bahrain After U.S.-Israeli Strikes</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/1/what-are-irans-weapons-as-it-fights-the-us-and-israel'>What are Iran’s weapons as it fights the US and Israel?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2dyz6p3weo'>What we know so far about the US-Israel attacks and Iran&#x27;s retaliation</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/01/iranian-strikes-hit-dubai-and-abu-dhabi-damaging-airport-terminals-and-the-burj-al-arab'>Iranian strikes hit Dubai and Abu Dhabi, damaging airport terminals and the Burj Al Arab</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-closes-embassy-in-iran-after-four-killed-in-attacks-across-the-gulf'>UAE closes embassy in Iran after four killed in attacks across the Gulf</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/dubai-abu-dhabi-live-updates-uae-shuts-tehran-embassy-airport-missiles-drones-attack-airspace-iran-israel-us-war-liveblog-13985221.html'>Dubai-Abu Dhabi News Live: Explosions heard across Gulf cities as Iran continues regional strikes</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uae-closes-embassy-in-iran-after-several-killed-in-attack